Project Rigger — methodology and decisions records archive (public tier)
========================================================================

What this is
------------
This repository is the archive tier of a workforce and talent framework
("Project Rigger") developed for the City of San Bruno. It holds historical
spine files (hash-chained records of architectural decisions) that have been
superseded by newer canonical versions but are preserved for chain-historical
auditability.

What this is not
----------------
- Not the active framework. The canonical, current-state framework lives in
  a private working surface (claude.ai project knowledge); this archive is
  the cold-storage complement.
- Not a complete record. Personal records, operational handoffs referencing
  specific stakeholders, and city-internal context live in a separate private
  archive repository.
- Not a substitute for executive function or staffing decisions.

Intent
------
The framework is published in part under CC BY 4.0 to allow reuse, citation,
and adaptation by other municipalities, civic-tech practitioners, and
methodology researchers. The records-keeping discipline (hash-chained
provenance, mod-N versioning, timestamped spine, etc.) is the substrate; the
specific San Bruno application is the worked example. Either is fair game
under the license, with attribution.

Provenance and integrity
------------------------
Each file in this archive is referenced from an `_archive_manifest.md` in the
canonical working surface with a SHA-256 hash captured at archive time.
Future audit operations can verify byte-equality between the manifest hash
and the file fetched from raw.githubusercontent.com.

